accessible take on baseball games.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >*Redistribution is strictly prohibited.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Simple Rules &amp; Terms (For First-Time Baseball Players)</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Strike</strong> = Missed hit.<br>3 strikes = 1 out.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Ball</strong> = Safe pitch (no swing).<br>4 balls = the batter goes to first base.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Out</strong> = Big mistake.<br>3 outs = switch offense and defense.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1 Inning</strong> = 1 turn.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1 Game</strong> = 9 innings.<br>If the score is tied after 9 innings, extra innings are played.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hit</strong> = Reach base and advance runners<br>according to the judgment panel shown in-game.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Run (Score)</strong> = A runner returns to home base.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Home Run</strong> = Instant score.<br>All runners on base also score.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >・You don’t need to remember these.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >・Just play once, and you’ll get it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You don’t need baseball knowledge — just click and play.</strong></p>",
